29:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-8","children":[["$","section","Who usually qualifies (high level)",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight","children":"Who usually qualifies (high level)"}],[["$","p","Lenders look at stable income, existing ",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Lenders look at stable income, existing EMIs, bureau score, and employment type. Salaried applicants with salary credits in a bank statement often clear faster than thin-file freelancers — but “guaranteed approval” WhatsApp ads are a red flag. RBI-regulated lenders must disclose key facts; read the Key Fact Statement before you e-sign."}],["$","p","Self-employed applicants are usually ask",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Self-employed applicants are usually asked for ITRs, business bank statements, and sometimes GST returns. Cool-off periods after a job change, bounced EMIs, and a burst of hard credit enquiries can all slow approval even when income looks fine on paper."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Age and citizenship / residency rules as stated by the lender",{"children":"Age and citizenship / residency rules as stated by the lender"}],["$","li","Minimum net income or salary credit history (often 3–6 months)",{"children":"Minimum net income or salary credit history (often 3–6 months)"}],["$","li","Bureau score and recent enquiry volume",{"children":"Bureau score and recent enquiry volume"}],["$","li","Existing EMI + proposed EMI under FOIR / debt-burden caps",{"children":"Existing EMI + proposed EMI under FOIR / debt-burden caps"}],["$","li","Stable employer / business vintage where the product requires it",{"children":"Stable employer / business vintage where the product requires it"}]]}],null,["$","div",null,{"className":"container flex justify-center py-4 !px-0","d