34:["$","section","EMI reality check before you apply",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight","children":"EMI reality check before you apply"}],[["$","p","Run the EMI on our calculator at the rat",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Run the EMI on our calculator at the rate and tenure the lender quotes — then add processing fee and insurance if bundled. Stress-test a 1–2% rate rise if the loan is floating. Prefer a gold loan only when you understand LTV and pledge risk (see our gold vs personal loan guide)."}],["$","p","A personal loan that “fits EMI” on paper",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"A personal loan that “fits EMI” on paper can still break cashflow after rent, school fees, and card minimums. Leave a buffer; do not borrow the maximum pre-approved limit just because the app shows it."}]],null,null,null]}]
35:["$","section","FOIR, CIBIL, and after-disbursal habits",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight","children":"FOIR, CIBIL, and after-disbursal habits"}],[["$","p","FOIR (fixed obligation to income) is the",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"FOIR (fixed obligation to income) is the lender’s view of how much income already goes to EMIs and similar obligations. Caps differ by bank and product. A strong bureau score helps pricing but does not erase a crowded FOIR."}],["$","p","After disbursal: autopay from the salary",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"After disbursal: autopay from the salary account, avoid stacking multiple personal loans in the same month, and do not ignore bounce charges. Multiple hard enquiries in a short window can suppress scores temporarily — apply when documents are ready, not “just to check”. Compare card vs personal loan if you are clearing revolving dues."}]],null,null,null]}]
36:["$","section","Red flags that are not “normal banking”",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight","children":"Red flags that are not “normal banking”"}],[["$","p","Anyone asking for advance fees to “unblo",{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Anyone asking for advance fees to “unblock” a loan, OTPs for your banking app, or KYC photos over WhatsApp is not a substitute for a regulated lender journey. Disburse only to your own account on the lender’s official channel."}]],null,null,null]}]
